From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Subject: mod-pcm-svc: link libm

mod_pcm_svc.c calls floor(), but src/makefile does not link libm. On
musl libm is part of libc, so it does not matter. On glibc the module
fails to load with "undefined symbol: floor", and every amx service
that imports mod_pcm_svc.odl exits at startup.

Add -lm to the LDFLAGS.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
--- a/src/makefile
+++ b/src/makefile
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 endif
 
 LDFLAGS += $(STAGING_LIBDIR) -shared -fPIC
-LDFLAGS += -lamxc -lamxp -lamxd -lamxo -lamxm -lamxj -lsahtrace
+LDFLAGS += -lamxc -lamxp -lamxd -lamxo -lamxm -lamxj -lsahtrace -lm
 
 # targets
 all: $(TARGET_SO)
